<!--
  The mark on a topic header whose own checkbox is ticked (schema v17's `task_groups.is_completed`).

  A 16dp box on the 24dp viewport, so it is the size of the caption line it stands beside rather than the 24dp of
  `ic_check_circle`, whose two existing users are both bigger marks: `TasksAdapter` puts it on a task row's selection
  box when the row is checked, and `item_goal_task.xml` tints it 24dp under `@color/status_done`. A mark that grows a
  text line to its own height is the failure Stage 15 found in the import preview, and the header has no vertical room
  to spare.

  The colour is the app's "finished" role (`status_done`, which resolves to `ink_success` and has its own night value),
  and it is the *third* channel, not the first: the sentence beside it and the strike through the topic's name both say
  the same thing without asking the reader to see a hue — which is why this drawable carries no accessible name of its
  own (§15).
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="16dp"
    android:height="16dp"
    android:viewportWidth="24"
    android:viewportHeight="24">
